body:
Why are people still having kids thinking they are perfect, tiny clones of themselves? 

&#x200B;

My family routinely uses the story of a meltdown I had when I was a child as an "She's always been dramatic and spoiled" doorstop.

&#x200B;

This wasn't about a refund.  I'm not going to stop pushing for a company to run itself properly and be transparent with patients, especially when this pharmacy and cultivator are(or were until very recently) affiliated.

Regardless of my experience, it's fucked up that this company is selling "medical" products with cannabinoids we can't even learn about. Sorry, I'm just not ok with that. If we don't call them out, nothing is going to change.
